@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] installed-export-native-proof
This fixture MUST exercise the installed restricted SSH module and source-built
channel, endpoint, permit and SSH client across separate NixOS machines using real
ZFS data. Synthetic enrollment and public-key distribution MUST NOT be reported
as Marshall coordination, destination adoption, guest migration or independent
physical-host acceptance. Listener interruption MUST prove the actual sender PID
is absent after source revocation succeeds; data EOF alone is not quiescence.


@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] source-revocation-live-listener
The typed source revocation effect MUST also be exercised while the SSH listener
remains active. Its receipt requires absence of the captured native sender PIDs;
subsequent use of the revoked credential MUST fail without yielding disk bytes.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] destination-fence-not-stream-receipt
Destination cancellation MUST erase/fence its key while a blocked native stream
still prevents a quiescence receipt. The fixture MUST distinguish this from source
sender revocation, then require stream lock release before accepting the destination
receipt. This check MUST NOT claim destination disk reclamation or guest migration.
